Subject: [PATCH] kwvk: report multiDrawIndirect

trynix carries this patch for kwvk, unkernel's guest Vulkan driver,
until unkernel takes it (pithings/unkernel#32, change 1).

GZDoom's ZVulkan takes a device only if it has samplerAnisotropy,
fragmentStoresAndAtomics, multiDrawIndirect and independentBlend
(libraries/ZVulkan/src/vulkanbuilders.cpp, FindDevices). kwvk reported
every one but multiDrawIndirect, with maxDrawIndirectCount 1, so GZDoom
found no device it accepts and fell back to GLES.

The renderer already draws any drawCount: vkCmdDrawIndirect and
vkCmdDrawIndexedIndirect loop over the records (js/core/vk-exec.ts).
The driver now reports the feature and 65535, the least
maxDrawIndirectCount the spec allows with it.

---
diff --git a/vk/icd/icd.c b/vk/icd/icd.c
index 42f7815..08f347b 100644
--- a/vk/icd/icd.c
+++ b/vk/icd/icd.c
@@ -365,7 +365,10 @@ static void pd_init(struct kw_physical_device *pd, struct kw_reply *rep)
 	l->subTexelPrecisionBits = 4;
 	l->mipmapPrecisionBits = 4;
 	l->maxDrawIndexedIndexValue = 0xffffffffu;
-	l->maxDrawIndirectCount = 1;
+	/* multiDrawIndirect: the renderer draws an indirect call's drawCount
+	 * records one by one (js/core/vk-exec.ts), so any count works; 2^16 - 1
+	 * is the least the spec allows with the feature */
+	l->maxDrawIndirectCount = 65535;
 	l->maxSamplerLodBias = 0;
 	l->maxSamplerAnisotropy = 16;
 	l->maxViewports = 1;
@@ -427,6 +430,7 @@ static void pd_init(struct kw_physical_device *pd, struct kw_reply *rep)
 	f->shaderClipDistance = HAS("clip-distances");
 	f->dualSrcBlend = HAS("dual-source-blending");
 	f->drawIndirectFirstInstance = HAS("indirect-first-instance");
+	f->multiDrawIndirect = 1;
 	f->occlusionQueryPrecise = 0;
 	pd->f16 = HAS("shader-f16");
 	if (HAS("timestamp-query")) {
